As of June 30, 2026, UDR owned or had an ownership position in 60,259 apartment homes, including 685 apartment homes under development. For over 54 years, UDR has delivered long-term value to shareholders, the best standard of service to residents and the highest quality experience for associates. UDR, Inc. was incorporated in 1972 in Maryland, and is based in Highlands Ranch, Colorado.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Thomas W. Toomey CPA | President, Chairman & CEO | Age 64 | Compensation: $923,318 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $1.2M ranks in the below the sector median among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 7%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $458K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $19K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["UDR, Inc. is a large-cap real estate business with a $13.2B market cap on $1.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are expanding by +3.3pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $650M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 38 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.39\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $3.5M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-3504808.0},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 10% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","38 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"UDR (UDR) Stock Still Looks Undervalued On Future Cash Flow","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nyse-udr/udr/news/udr-udr-stock-still-looks-unde